+## 1. Extension and configuration contracts
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add manifest/schema support for generic CLI entry metadata and extension scope.
+- [x] 1.2 Add core APIs for user-owned extension config files, including `config-monitor.yaml` path, safe YAML read/write, and upgrade/卸载保留 semantics.
+- [x] 1.3 Remove Monitor from core init-generated configuration while retaining a non-destructive legacy migration path.
+
+## 2. Hook protocol separation
+
+- [x] 2.1 Split Provider-neutral event extraction from write-protection-only tool classification and decision helpers.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement independent Monitor observer runner and Codex/Claude observer commands with failure-open acknowledgement.
+- [x] 2.3 Add independent Hook composition markers, install/uninstall handling, and dependency-isolation tests.
+
+## 3. Monitor extension packaging
+
+- [x] 3.1 Move Monitor Store, HTTP server, page, assets, i18n and reporter into `extensions/monitor/0.1.0` without changing business behavior.
+- [x] 3.2 Add Monitor manifest, init/runtime/CLI entrypoints, `config-monitor.yaml` default template, and package integrity metadata.
+- [x] 3.3 Migrate existing Monitor tests to extension runtime behavior and add multi-Workspace/global runtime coverage.
+
+## 4. Generic extension CLI
+
+- [x] 4.1 Register and parse static `code-w ext` command with `--` argument passthrough and workspace/global scope resolution.
+- [x] 4.2 Implement core CLI host execution, hash/timeout/exit validation, result envelope, diagnostics, and stable errors.
+- [x] 4.3 Route legacy `code-w monitor` to `code-w ext monitor` as a compatibility alias.
+
+## 5. Migration, verification, and cleanup
+
+- [x] 5.1 Migrate legacy `config.monitor` and Monitor Hook entries atomically, preserving write-protection/user entries.
+- [x] 5.2 Remove core Monitor imports, managed assets, config projection and initialization branches after compatibility coverage is in place.
+- [x] 5.3 Add CLI architecture, rollback, stale-plan, config-isolation, and observer/write-protection independence tests; run full check and packaging validation.
